NAME
    Mojolicious::Plugin::FormRequest - Laravel-style form request validation
    for Mojolicious

SYNOPSIS
      # In your application
      $app->plugin('FormRequest', dbh => $dbh);

      # In a controller
      my $data = $c->validate('UserCreate') or return;

      # In lib/MyApp/Validation/UserCreate.pm
      package MyApp::Validation::UserCreate;
      sub rules {
          return {
              name  => ['required', ['size', 2, 50]],
              email => ['required', ['like', qr/^[^@]+@[^@]+$/],
                        ['unique', 'users', 'email']],
          };
      }
      sub messages {
          return { 'email.unique' => 'This email is already registered' };
      }
      1;

DESCRIPTION
    Validation rules live in dedicated Perl classes. On failure the plugin
    responds automatically: JSON 422 for JSON requests, flash + redirect
    for HTML requests. On success, validated data (only declared fields)
    is returned.

OPTIONS
    dbh         DBI handle. Required for unique/exists checks.
    namespace   Namespace for validation classes. Defaults to
                "<moniker>::Validation".
    fail_fast   Stop at the first error. Default false.

INSTALLATION
    cpanm Mojolicious::Plugin::FormRequest

LICENSE
    Same terms as Perl itself.
